The next round of the Outreachy open source internship program
(https://www.outreachy.org/) runs from December 5, 2017 to March 5,
2018.  Internships are 12-week projects that consist of paid,
full-time, remote work contributing to open source projects.

Regular QEMU contributors are invited to participate as mentors.  A
mentor helps their intern contribute by answering questions, reviewing
code, and giving feedback.  This usually involves around 5 hours of
volunteer work per week for a mentor.

Mentoring is fun and rewarding.  If you'd like to find out more, check
out this presentation on open source internships:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xNVCX7YMUL8

The application period for interns opens on September 7th.  Please
post project ideas on the wiki:
https://wiki.qemu.org/Outreachy_2017_DecemberMarch

If you have any questions, please let me know.

Stefan
